Agent: Mandatory before claiming hot-path perf wins. Apply when changing parse, FilterEngine, Lua, gnet, RTB, edge ingress, load tests, or BPF collector.

Hot-path perf gate (summary)

Validate with both reports in `var/load-test/<UTC-ts>/`:

1. Prometheus — `bottleneck-report.md`: handler p95/p99, `ad_worker_pool_reject_total` (0), fraud stream drops, Redis Lua p99 < 10 ms/shard.
2. BPF — `bpf-report.md`: k6 on-CPU share, cgroup throttle %, tracker `epoll_wait`/`read`/`futex` p99, peak FDs.

Preflight: `prepare_constrained_stack.sh` → `make bpf-dev` → `sudo ESPX_BPF_PROBE=1 bash scripts/load-test/run_dirty_load.sh business`.

After code change: `make test-alloc-gate`; re-run load+BPF when touching filter order, parse, worker pool, or Lua args.

Load-test BPF probes and kernel analytics

Dev-only observability for laptop and staging load tests. Complements Prometheus (`bottleneck-report.md`) with host-kernel signals: syscall latency, scheduler runqueue, cgroup throttle, FD/socket growth, and honest k6 generator overhead.

Not production edge XDP (`.cursor/rules/edge.mdc`). The object `deploy/dev/bpf/loadtest_probe.o` is never loaded by `tracker`, `nginx`, or CI.

Goals

Is k6 saturating the laptop CPU?: BPF — k6 on-CPU %, ctx/s, RSS delta; Prometheus — k6 VUs, dropped iterations (k6 log)
Is tracker waiting on epoll/Redis?: BPF — `epoll_wait` / `read` / `write` p99 per role; Prometheus — `ad_http_request_duration_seconds`, Redis Lua histogram
Are compose CPU limits biting?: BPF — cgroup `cpu.stat` throttle %; Prometheus — container CPU in Grafana
Connection / thread leak under load?: BPF — peak FDs, `socket()` rate, thread fork/exit; Prometheus — `ad_gnet_*`, worker rejects
Network retry on loopback?: BPF — TCP retrans per process; Prometheus — Redis timeout metrics

Use both reports from the same run directory: `var/load-test/<timestamp>/`.

Architecture

```text
run_dirty_load.sh / run_spike_load.sh
  ├─ k6 → nginx → tracker (application path)
  └─ bpf_probe_session.sh start
        ├─ bpf_resolve_targets.sh  → bpf/targets.json (container PIDs)
        ├─ bpf-collector (root/CAP_BPF)
        │     ├─ loadtest_probe.o  tracepoints (syscalls, sched, TCP)
        │     ├─ /proc sampler     FDs, threads, faults (2s)
        │     └─ cgroup sampler    cpu.stat, memory.current (2s)
        └─ bpf_probe_session.sh stop
              └─ analyze_bpf.sh → bpf-report.md
                    └─ analyze_bottlenecks.sh links bpf-report.md when present
```

Components

`deploy/dev/bpf/loadtest_probe.bpf.c`: CO-RE BPF program: syscall enter/exit, sched wake/switch, TCP retrans, slow-event ringbuf
`deploy/dev/bpf/common/espx_probe.h`: Shared map layouts and histogram keys
`cmd/bpf-collector/`: Go loader: attach probes, aggregate maps, write session artifacts
`scripts/load-test/bpf_build.sh`: Build `.o` via host `clang` or Docker
`scripts/load-test/bpf_requirements.sh`: Preflight: BTF, root/tracing, `go`, optional `bpftool`
`scripts/load-test/bpf_resolve_targets.sh`: Map compose container names → host PIDs + roles
`scripts/load-test/bpf_probe_session.sh`: Start/stop collector around k6
`scripts/load-test/analyze_bpf.sh`: Render `bpf-report.md` from `bpf/maps/summary.json`

Quick start

```bash
# One-time build (also: make bpf-dev, dev_stack.sh bpf, or dev_stack.sh build)
bash scripts/local-dev/bpf_setup.sh
# equivalent:
bash scripts/load-test/bpf_build.sh
go build -o bin/bpf-collector ./cmd/bpf-collector

# Constrained stack + business mix (prepares DB/registry, 2m, 50/20/30 traffic)
sudo ESPX_BPF_PROBE=1 bash scripts/load-test/run_dirty_load.sh business

# Smoke with lighter syscall sampling on laptops
sudo ESPX_BPF_PROBE=1 ESPX_BPF_SAMPLE_RATE=10 bash scripts/load-test/run_dirty_load.sh smoke
```

Standalone session (no k6 — staging traffic, curl, vegeta):

```bash
make bpf-dev
sudo make bpf-session-start          # or: dev_stack.sh probe start
# generate traffic...
sudo make bpf-session-stop
bash scripts/local-dev/bpf_session.sh report
```

Defaults for standalone (`bpf_session.sh start`): `ESPX_BPF_NATIVE=1`, periodic dump/refresh every 30s, live metrics on `:9464`.

Requires root or passwordless `sudo` (BPF attach + memlock). Optional: `ESPX_BPF_SUDO_PASS` for non-interactive sudo.

Artifacts:

```text
